# Sensors

Demonstrates how to configure `PointerSensor` and `KeyboardSensor`. Use the toggle buttons to switch between sensor modes at runtime.

For keyboard mode: focus any item with **Tab**, then press **Enter** or **Space** to pick it up. Use **arrow keys** to navigate, **Enter** to drop, **Escape** to cancel.

<SensorsExample />

```ts
import {
    DndController,
    PointerSensor,
    KeyboardSensor,
} from '@horuse/svelte-dnd';

// Both sensors (default)
const controller = new DndController({
    sensors: [new PointerSensor(), new KeyboardSensor(controller)],
});

// Pointer only — disables keyboard drag
const controller = new DndController({
    sensors: [new PointerSensor()],
});

// Keyboard only — disables pointer drag
const controller = new DndController({
    sensors: [new KeyboardSensor(controller)],
});
```

See [Sensors docs](/docs/sensors) for the full API reference.
